WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.370
We have some real problems
in this country that

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.790
are deep and structural
that have to be confronted

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.850
with the truth of who we are.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.750
CORNEL WEST: I invite
each and every one of you

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.980
listen to these
different voices.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.800
Have the courage
to say, "Hmm, let

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.120
me see what this wrestling with
white supremacy and Black love

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.340
is all about."

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:30.030
In this class, we are
going to be focusing

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.830
on these powerful issues.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.670
Together--

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.128
NIKOLE HANNAH-JONES:
You will learn

00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:36.390
how slavery and
anti-blackness is

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.390
foundational to nearly
every American institution

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.450
in modern life even if
we refuse to see it.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.210
JELANI COBB: You may hear things
that you find hard to believe.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.970
They are a testament
to parts of our history

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.230
that we've dismissed.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.690
The story that you can
tell about this country,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.000
about it being a land of
equality and opportunity,

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.650
who gave America that?

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.955
We gave America that.

00:00:57.955 --> 00:01:02.080
There has been this
unbroken history of struggle

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.160
for liberation for
hundreds of years.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.970
Black people manage
to create beauty

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.745
in the very process of
fighting structural racism.

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:16.120
KIMBERLÉ WILLIAMS CRENSHAW:
Black love is that thing that

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.810
makes you believe in American
democracy even when American

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.210
democracy hasn't believed in us.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.710
JOHN MCWHORTER:
One of our jobs is

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:26.770
to try to make there be as
little racism as possible.

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.290
A more important
job is to see where

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.650
the racism is and think about
ways that we can get past it.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.390
Race is a fiction.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.010
Racism is real.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.320
What do we do with that?

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.300
And it's only in having
that understanding of what

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.600
built the country that we're
in that we can dismantle

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.240
the parts of our country that
don't live up to its highest

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.061
ideals.

00:01:48.061 --> 00:01:49.255
 I'm John McWhorter.

00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:50.695
 I'm Sherrilyn Ifill.

00:01:50.695 --> 00:01:51.775
 I'm Jelani Cobb.

00:01:51.775 --> 00:01:52.870
 Nikole Hannah-Jones.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.565
 Kimberlé Williams Crenshaw.

00:01:54.565 --> 00:01:56.020
 Cornel West.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.450
 I'm Angela Davis, and
this is MasterClass.

